{{also|Buddy}}
{{wikipedia|dab=buddy}}
==English==

===Etymology===
* Colloquial ''butty'' (1802), meaning [[companion]], also the form of an older dialect term meaning [[workmate]], associated with coal mining.  Itself believed derived from ''booty fellow'' (1530), a partner with whom one shares [[booty]] or [[loot]]. [http://www.etymonline.com/index.php?term=buddy]

* Sometimes referred to in North American dictionaries as an alteration of [[brother]].

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/bʌ.di/|lang=en}}
* {{audio|En-us-buddy.ogg|Audio (US)}}
* {{rhymes|ʌdi}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|buddies}}

# A [[friend]] or [[casual]] acquaintance.
#: ''They have been '''buddies''' since they were in school.''
# A [[partner]] for a particular activity.
#: ''drinking '''buddies'''''
# An [[informal]] and friendly address to a [[stranger]]; a friendly [[placeholder]] name for a person one does not know.
#: ''Hey, '''buddy''', I think you dropped this.''

====Synonyms====
* {{qualifier|friend or acquaintance}}: [[mate]]
* {{qualifier|address to a stranger}}: [[mate]]

* See also [[Wikisaurus:friend]]

====Derived terms====
* [[buddy store]]
* [[buddy system]]
* [[buddy up]]
* [[Buddyroll]]
* [[fuck buddy]]

